Z||000000||TRiAD||11-30-2001||07:44 PM||||I recieved an email from "_dmkfiero@ovis.net" that Outlook blocked, due to possible dangerous attatchments...<P>I thought nothing of it, and attempted to reply, to tell him (or her) to re-send as a different file type, and I got a deliver failure notification. <P>It sounds like someone is using our family to propogate a virus...beware...<BR>||||reg||4
Z||000001||Jay||11-30-2001||07:50 PM||||I got something similar but not from that email address.  Don't open anything you're not expecting!<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig2_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||avengador1||11-30-2001||07:53 PM||||I got an email from bmwracer out of ebay saying that his computer had gotten a virus and might have sent it to me unknowingly. Im behind a firewall but I checked anyway. Didn't find anything. No infection.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||pherder||11-30-2001||08:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TRiAD:<BR><B>I recieved an email from "_dmkfiero@ovis.net" that Outlook blocked, due to possible dangerous attatchments...<P>I thought nothing of it, and attempted to reply, to tell him (or her) to re-send as a different file type, and I got a deliver failure notification. <P>It sounds like someone is using our family to propogate a virus...beware...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>If you noticed ... the email address was changed by the virus(worm/whatever) to have a "_" in front of the REAL email address.<P>So if you email "dmkfiero@ovis.net" leaving out the leading "_" you will send to the person who has the virus!<P>I have gotten 3 in one day from 3 different people.  None of which knew that their computer was infected.  All had their email return address modified with the leading "_".<P>Two of the messages were "PIF" files, the other was a "SCR" file.  I didn't open any of the attachments.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Paul<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||CoolBlue87GT||11-30-2001||08:17 PM||||OH YES, I know what your talking about.<P>My computer got a virus from the email greeting card company.  -- (I think.)<P>I sent out a greeting to friends, and not knowingly sent them a virus.<P>It was named something like win32.Badtrans.29020  -  supposted to be a new & really bad virus. It sends to all in the address book, without any knowledge of the user.<P>I got messages from companies Maryland & and Ft. Worth that my computer had sent them an email with a virus.<P>My virus program did not detect it !<P>I now have a different virus program in place.<P>You all might want to invest in an updated copy of a virus check program.<P>- I had McAfee Vshield , still let it run in the backround.<P>Now I use InoculateIT Real-Time for internet protection, and for e-mail "Mail Watcher"<P>I hate those that 'get off' on creating these virus programs. ||||reg||9
Z||000005||Oreif||11-30-2001||09:56 PM||||Read thru this thread.<BR>It has links to which virus it is and how it got spread thru the Fiero message board at Fiero.org.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/012259.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/012259.html</A> ||||reg||4
Z||000006||Cheever3000||11-30-2001||11:13 PM||||I switched a long time ago from McAfee to Norton because I wasn't confident McAfee would get everything.  Norton has done a good job for me.  It caught the Badtrans attachment that I too received from DMK.<P>If anybody gets one from me, I hope they'll tell me about it.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Raydar||12-01-2001||01:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cheever3000:<BR><B>I switched a long time ago from McAfee to Norton because I wasn't confident McAfee would get everything...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>McAfee didn't play well with my 'puter. Made it do funny things.<P>I use Norton at home and we use Norton at work, as well. <BR>Gotta remember to keep those virus definitions updated, though. Otherwise, it's useless.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
